      "observed": "The netlist places every MCU VDD pin in unconnected nets. It also leaves NAVC1 VSS pins tied only to each other in Net-(NAVC1-VSS-Pad18), and NAVC1 VSSA is unconnected rather than tied to GND.",
      "expected": "The specification states that the 3V3 rail feeds both MCUs, and standard MCU practice requires all VDD pins to be connected to the 3.3 V supply and all VSS/VSSA pins to ground.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "source": "netlist",
          "quote": "(net (code \"216\") (name \"unconnected-(FCC1-VDD-Pad11)\") (node (ref \"FCC1\") (pin \"11\") (pinfunction \"VDD\") (pintype \"power_in\")))"
        },
        {
          "source": "netlist",
          "quote": "(net (code \"92\") (name \"Net-(NAVC1-VSS-Pad18)\") (node (ref \"NAVC1\") (pin \"18\") (pinfunction \"VSS\") (pintype \"power_in\")) (node (ref \"NAVC1\") (pin \"63\") (pinfunction \"VSS\") (pintype \"passive\")))"
        },
        {
          "source": "spec",
          "quote": "3V3 feeds both MCUs (FCC, NAVC) and all I2C sensor ICs"
        }
      ],
      "impact": "Both MCUs are effectively unpowered, and the NAVC ground reference is floating, so the flight controller cannot boot or operate.",
      "confidence": 0.98
    },
